# Android emulator testing

Use the existing AVD `OneVelox_API35`. Do not create a new AVD unless that one is missing.

Always use Android Studio JBR, never system Java 8:

- `ANDROID_HOME` = `C:\Users\rtd19\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk`
- `JAVA_HOME` = `C:\Program Files\Android\Android Studio\jbr`

Run via `tools/emulator-run.ps1` with `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass`. Default flavor is `beta` (`com.onevelox.app.beta`, location simulation on).

```
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/emulator-run.ps1 run
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/emulator-run.ps1 logs
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/emulator-run.ps1 screenshot
```

The user watches the emulator window. The agent must capture logcat (`FATAL EXCEPTION`, `AndroidRuntime`, `*:E`) and a screenshot under `%TEMP%\onevelox-emulator`, then fix crashes found there. Do not stop the emulator unless asked. Shell commands need unsandboxed/`all` permissions on this Windows machine.
